# The JVM's own numbers: opcodes, class-file version, array type codes and
# access flags. One definition each, because there is only one JVM.
#
# They used to live wherever they were first needed -- codegen, emit and
# testrun each grew their own block, and eight opcodes ended up declared twice
# with (fortunately) the same value. Nothing would have caught a typo in the
# second copy: an opcode is an integer, and the wrong integer is a different
# instruction that the verifier may well accept. ARCH-05's third suggestion in
# docs/codebase-audit.md is this file.
#
# The values are the JVM Specification's, chapter 6 (opcodes), 4.1 (version,
# access flags) and 6.5's newarray atype table. `use jvmops.{...}` selectively:
# a module lists the instructions it emits, which reads as a summary of what it
# does.

# ---- access flags (JVMS 4.1) ----
pub const ACC_ABSTRACT: Int = 1024
pub const ACC_FINAL: Int = 16
pub const ACC_INTERFACE: Int = 512
pub const ACC_PRIVATE: Int = 2
pub const ACC_PROTECTED: Int = 4
pub const ACC_PUBLIC: Int = 1
pub const ACC_STATIC: Int = 8
pub const ACC_VOLATILE: Int = 64

# ---- class-file version (JVMS 4.1) ----

## The major version every emitted class carries.
##
## 49 is deliberate and it is a floor, not a preference (docs/jvm-base-plan.md
## K-A4). Below major 50 the JVM verifies by type inference and asks for no
## StackMapTable at all, which is how the frames disappear; at 50 and above
## they are mandatory. Below 49 `ldc` of a class constant is not allowed, and
## `cast` emits one. So 49 is the only version that buys the frames back.
##
## Nothing else here may exceed it: a method-handle or method-type entry in
## the constant pool is a parse error at this version even when unreachable,
## which is why the closure classes came first (K-A3) and why
## scripts/constpool-scan.py guards the pool.
pub const V49: Int = 49

## The ClassWriter flag that goes with it: COMPUTE_MAXS, not COMPUTE_FRAMES.
##
## The version alone saves nothing. Asked to compute frames at 49, ASM writes
## the pre-StackMapTable `StackMap` attribute instead, which is larger than
## what it replaces and which the JVM then ignores. Only this flag stops it.
pub const COMPUTE_MAXS: Int = 1

# ---- newarray atype codes (JVMS 6.5) ----
pub const T_BYTE: Int = 8
pub const T_INT: Int = 10

